class_name AlphaNotes
extends RefCounted

## JON'S TWO NOTES TO ALPHA PLAYERS, in his own words. Both are exempt from the
## plain-voice rewrite and the reading-grade cap: leave them as written. A blank
## line is a paragraph break; the signature is its own line.
##
## ALPHA_WELCOME: the welcome popup (`WelcomePopup`), shown once per profile at
## the title screen and again from its MESSAGE FROM JON line.
## ALPHA_THANKS: the win screen (`GameOverScreen`), when the core's boss is beaten.

const ALPHA_WELCOME := """Welcome to the Three Kelvin Alpha!

This is an early alpha of the game I have always wanted to play, a game that has only existed in pieces scattered across many others. It is my attempt to make the game of my dreams, and it draws inspiration from the games of my youth and the modern games I love.

A special shoutout to my friend James Barney, who spent a lot of time building the foundational systems you will use throughout the game, and who helped keep the GitHub repository from being a total mess. This was certainly not a solo project.

Thank you so much for giving my silly little game a try, and for putting up with the many bugs you will find in this early build. I would love to hear your thoughts, favorite moments, constructive criticism, any bugs you run into, and anything you would love to see in the final game.

<3

Jon"""

const ALPHA_THANKS := """You have reached the end of the Three Kelvin Alpha! If you are reading this, you made it all the way to the core and defeated the final boss.

From the bottom of my heart, thank you so much for playing my silly little game, and for putting up with the bugs and weird things that come with an unfinished game.

As I mentioned in the welcome message, please reach out to me with bugs, ideas and feature requests. Tell me what you liked and what you didn't like.

Thanks again for helping me build the game of my dreams.

<3

Jon"""
